<title>USA: CTG's Hartford Steam set cooling peak.</title>
<headline>CTG's Hartford Steam set cooling peak.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD, Conn. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>CTG Resources Inc on Friday said Hartford Steam Co, its district heating and cooling operation, set a new system cooling peak on Tuesday, July 14.</p>
<p>Its output was 25,128 tons of cooling to meet the air-conditioning needs of 46 large customers in the Hartford, Connecticut, system and 14 customers in the capital city area during what was a week of hot and humid weather.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
